# Turn-controller fix — verification log (30.10, desk)

> Scope: spin-turn under-rotation/asymmetry debugged to root cause in
> `lab1_stage7_faultrecovery.ino` (turn machine byte-identical to frozen
> stage 4/5/6). Straight controller, protocol, ISR layer, stage-7 fault
> layer: UNTOUCHED. Stage-6/5/4/3/2 sketch files: UNTOUCHED.
> All numbers below are real tool output (MSYS2 g++ + the _hostcheck
> virtual-robot harness), exit codes checked.

== BASELINE reproduction (pre-fix binary) ==
build: OK, 1 warning (pre-existing wheelTargetMM unused, same as frozen)
[diag probe, L90 in the harness]
  tturn cmd=L90.0 got=77.5deg L=-20cnt R=20cnt coast=-2cnt     (sketch odometry)
  [sim] pose heading=97.6deg | ticks L=-26 R=26                 (ground truth)
  -> the sketch UNDER-reports its own rotation by ~20 deg; the robot's
     real runs (69.8-71.7 deg on L90) show the same signature PLUS plant
     asymmetry on top. sim_fault S8 pre-fix: got=79.5 (old band 75-80 =
     the artifact banded as "expected" - band corrected this session).
[telemetry through the stop, pre-fix]
  tel prog=89.2 rem=0.8deg pwm=86  ->  tturn got=77.5
  -> 11.7 deg of ALREADY-COUNTED rotation vanish between the last control
     step and the result line. Lost AFTER the stop condition, in odometry.

== ROOT CAUSE (three stacked defects, all in the post-stop turn path) ==
1. stopTurn() fired an unconditional powered REVERSE kick (driveReverse,
   KICK_PWM 95 / KICK_MS 60). driveReverse re-stamps dirL/dirR (isrL/isrR
   sign edges by COMMANDED direction, .ino:215/222) while the wheels are
   still spinning in the ORIGINAL direction -> every residual edge counts
   BACKWARD. This is the constant per-turn deficit (angle-independent).
2. the fold arithmetic double-counted the entire post-stop interval:
   settlePhase()/T_KICK did coastL += encCountL() - coastSnapL, but
   encCountL() is the LIVE counter that already contains that interval
   -> final = drive + 2*(kick+coast). Sign-chaotic after defect 1.
   (On the real robot this produced the "asymmetry": |R fwd| > |L back|,
   sum NL+NR != 0 - the reported wheels disagreed with physical rotation.)
3. the T_KICK->T_COAST handoff never refreshed lastCtrlMs, so after a
   stop the 50 Hz scheduler starved turnStep until a queued straight
   command re-armed the clock (masked in 1-command tests, visible in routes).

H1 (e=(NL-NR) instead of NL+NR): REFUTED - .ino:851 uses (|cL|-|cR|),
    magnitude equalisation, correct polarity for both wheel signs.
H2 (symmetry not called): REFUTED - M_SPIN branch at .ino:849 runs every
    T_RUN step; symGain initialised K_SYM 3.0 (.ino:278).
H3 (turnDone coasts): REFUTED - all turn exits call brake() (.ino:660/696/741);
    coast() is called only in setup() and the operator 'c' abort (.ino:256).
H4 (stage-7 fault layer in turns): REFUTED - detectors arm ONLY in
    beginDrive() (.ino:371); turnStart() never arms; loop() routes turns
    to turnStep() only (.ino:1166-1170). Turn PWM floor 85 = PWM_MIN by
    design, same floor the detector margins were calibrated around.
ROOT CAUSE = defects 1+2+3 above (stop-kick sign flip + double-counted
folds + scheduler starvation). The prompt's (a)/(b)/(c) subset: (a) the
spin error FORMULA was already correct (no change needed - documented),
(b) brake() was already called (the powered kick ON TOP of brake() was
the bug - removed), (c) stage-7 was never active in turns (no change
needed - documented).

== THE FIX (turnStep machine only; +1 tunable, TURN_-prefixed per rules) ==
- stopTurn(): brake() ONLY, no driveReverse kick; stop-instant snapshot
  (stopSnapL/R) kept for the coast= diagnostic; settle-poll tracker
  (coastSnapL/R) refreshed (never folded) so QUIET_MS/COAST_TMO still work.
- settlePhase()/T_KICK folds DELETED: live counters are the whole truth.
- turnStep(): lastCtrlMs = millis() on EVERY phase (shared-clock fix).
- stop condition: rem <= STOP_TOL_DEG + TURN_STOP_LEAD_DEG (lead 7.8 deg =
  measured brake residual 2 count-pairs + stop-step overshoot at the
  PWM_MIN floor; recipe in the constant comment; 1 pair = 3.878 deg).
- overshoot correction kick RETAINED but only from the settle phase AFTER
  quiet (dir re-stamp harmless on still wheels) - now rare by construction.
- coast= field now reports the honest post-stop residual (already inside
  got=; information only).
- telemetry hook behind #if defined(TELEMETRY_TURN) && TELEMETRY_TURN:
  tturn_tel tgt_ticks/NL/NR/pwmL/pwmR/e/corr once per T_RUN step. NOT
  defined for acceptance builds (verified: undefined build has zero
  tel output; -DTELEMETRY_TURN=1 build compiles clean and streams).

== target_ticks math (alternative root cause, ruled out) ==
theta(rad) = 90 * pi/180 = 1.5708; per-wheel arc = b*theta/2 =
151 * 1.5708 / 2 = 118.60 mm; target_ticks = 118.60 / K_MM 5.1087 =
23.2 counts. Firmware: wheelTargetMM() = track*rad/2 (identical formula,
only unused because turnStep drives by deg directly - same 23.2 target
lands via rem <= tol). Robot data: healthy pairs land on 23.2 cnt grids
(46.4/2 = 23.2) - matches.

